From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:07:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Follow WPT ed5a113c's corner-shape reference contours

WPT rewrote css-borders/corner-shape/resources/render-corner-shape.js
after 6efb1b12, and the reftests compare against that file. The old port
moved inner edges along one normal derived from the half-corner point and
pinned the ends with a control-point line, so concave corners (scoop,
notch, superellipse(-2), superellipse(-7)) with thick borders painted a
different padding edge from the new reference.

The contour now follows the new corner_clip_out_path: per-end normals
skewed by the difference between the two insets, miters for negative
insets, a self-intersection cut for large outsets of concave corners, a
quarter ellipse between the tangents for -1 < k < 0, and the
css-backgrounds-3 spread adjustment for radii smaller than an outset.
Points past the moved rect are now clipped where each segment crosses an
edge instead of only clamped, because the new end points sit outside the
rect, and clamping a slanted segment moved its crossing.

Blitz upstream does not paint corner-shape at all; this only affects the
Kitesurf port.
